# Documentation and Phase Closure

Every implementation phase or material product slice **must update `README.md`
before that phase can be declared complete.**

`README.md` is the current product baseline. It must always reflect:

- the current completed phase
- major implemented capabilities
- architecture and security changes that landed in that phase
- new migrations relevant to the current baseline
- test/verification status from a run in this workspace (never historical
  assumed counts)
- intentionally unsupported / out-of-scope functionality
- known verification gaps (including browser QA not run)

## Verdicts

A phase **must not** receive a final PASS / VERIFIED / CLOSED verdict while
`README.md` still describes an older product baseline (for example, calling the
repo Phase 4 after Tasks exist).

Do not claim browser QA passed unless an interactive walkthrough was actually
performed in this session. If browser tools were unavailable, say so.

Do not start the next numbered phase until `README.md` matches the code that
just shipped.
